# Plans must aim past current Forja

Index: [expert-first](./expert-first.mdc) (Q&A recommend first). This rule covers **plans / RFCs / issue designs**.

When the user asks for a **plan**, design the **better** architecture / API / UX. Current Forja is the baseline to improve — not the ceiling, and not physics.

## Three layers (required in capability tables)

| Layer | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **Platform / library** | What Exo Media3, mpv, Android, etc. allow |
| **Forja today** | What we wire now |
| **Plan target** | What this plan builds |

## Forbidden

- “Not today”, “no”, “can’t”, “fixed at build” as the **only** answer for a capability when the library allows a better approach
- Letting status quo freeze the design as if the platform forbids the fix

## Required

Lead with the better approach. Put the Forja gap in a baseline column or one short clause. Gap → fix is always one line of **target design** (e.g. mutable custom `LoadControl` + `setLiveCushion`), not “we don’t do X yet.”

```
Wrong: Exo | No today — DefaultLoadControl fixed at build
Right: Exo | Mutable custom LoadControl (Media3) — Forja still uses fixed DefaultLoadControl; plan adds runtime caps
```
